retrievalContext:
6.5 Business model tests
The RM must be able to state, in three sentences or fewer, how the business makes money, who pays it, and why customers will keep paying it. If not, the application is not ready for credit. Credit must decline where the business model:
- depends on a single contract or customer > 50% of revenue without contractual protection beyond the loan tenor, unless approved by Senior Credit Manager;
- has no evidenced path to positive operating cash flow within the facility tenor (outside Start-up policy);
- relies on regulatory permissions the business does not hold.

