retrievalContext:
10.2 CFADS methodology
\text{CFADS} = \text{Normalised EBITDA} - \text{Cash tax} - \text{Maintenance capex} - \Delta\text{Working capital} - \text{Sustainable owner drawings}
\text{DSCR} = \frac{\text{CFADS}}{\text{Scheduled principal} + \text{Interest} + \text{Lease and HP payments}}
Normalised EBITDA, Policy treatment = Section 10.4. Use the lower of last full-year and LTM where management accounts show deterioration. Cash tax, Policy treatment = Tax actually payable on the normalised profit, not the P&L charge. For sole traders and partnerships, deduct the principals' income tax and NIC on business profits. Maintenance capex, Policy treatment = The higher of (i) the 3-year average capex excluding identified growth capex and (ii) 50% of annual depreciation. Growth capex funded by new debt is excluded. Δ Working capital, Policy treatment = The investment needed to support forecast revenue at current working-capital days. Releases of working capital from falling sales are not counted as CFADS. Sustainable owner drawings, Policy treatment = For companies: dividends required to cover directors' personal living costs where salary has been normalised to below that level, minimum £30k per working owner (illustrative). For sole traders/partners: actual drawings, minimum £30k per working principal. Debt service, Policy treatment = All scheduled payments to all lenders over the next 12 months, including HP and lease rentals, the proposed facility on its contractual profile, and RCF interest assuming 50% average utilisation (100% if historically > 75% utilised). Interest rate, Policy treatment = Contractual rate for fixed debt. Floating debt at the current reference rate plus margin, plus the policy stress in Section 14

